
<p>Chance Miller, 9to5Mac:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Flighty’s new Connection Assistant feature includes step-by-step
information for your specific connection. This includes things
like terminal changes, security checkpoints, passport control, and
more. Connection Assistant also gives you estimates of how long
each step of making a connection usually takes.</p>

<p>“The new Connection Assistant combines Flighty’s best-in-class
flight tracking data with airport-specific procedures and
statistical modeling of millions of prior flights, and then turns
it all into guidance for your exact trip,” the Flighty team
explained in a <a href="https://docs.craft.do/editor/d/a89c6d38-642e-8105-e733-9c434670c92d/7548402b-cf3f-4f0f-97a5-b064e2eae53c?s=ZH1ghei9FDddBnK4k6Q3R5xLCTukRr2wWjERBd6VJYc7">press release</a> today.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>I don’t know what the equivalent term to “Mac-assed” should be for iPhone apps, but whatever it is, Flighty epitomizes it. Incredibly useful for what it does, exemplary for how it looks and feels and is visually organized. It is as iOS-assed as an app can be.</p>

